{% raw %}<section class="band band-photo"><img src="/images/2021/08/4mls-hero.webp" alt="Open kitchen and living room with a long island and lake views" width="1024" height="683" fetchpriority="high" class="band-img"></section><section class="band"><div class="wrap"><div class="el-row" style="--cols:50fr 50fr"><div class="el-col"><h1>Kitchen Countertops  New Orleans &amp; the Northshore</h1><div class="el-text"><p>Countertops set the tone for your entire kitchen. Along with cabinets, they are the design decision that shapes everything else including the color palette, the texture &amp; the feel of the space. At Singer Kitchens, we help you choose the right material, the right finish and the right fit for how you actually live in your kitchen.</p></div><div class="el-text"><p>Singer Kitchens offers one of the best selections of countertop materials in Greater New Orleans. With a wide selection of in-stock stones available and priced by the square foot. You pay only for what you use, not for the whole the slab.</p></div><p class="btn-row"><a class="btn" href="/request-consultation/">Request a Design Conversation</a></p></div><div class="el-col"><figure class="el-img"><img src="/images/2025/03/05mls.webp" alt="Wood cabinet kitchen with a peninsula and herringbone floor" width="1200" height="800" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></figure></div></div></div></section><section class="band"><div class="wrap"><h1>Expert Guidance in Choosing the Right Countertops</h1><div class="el-text"><p>Countertop choices go well beyond color and material. There are price options, durability considerations and lifestyle factors that all play a role. Our designers are knowledgeable across all countertop types, styles and materials. They will help you find what works for your kitchen and your budget.</p></div><div class="el-text"><p>We have over 75 in-stock stones available by the square foot including granite, quartz, quartzite and more. Because you are purchasing by the square foot rather than by the slab, you only pay for the stone you actually use. That is a meaningful cost difference, especially on smaller projects.</p></div><div class="el-text">We also carry a wide selection of undermount sinks to complement whichever countertop material you choose.</div></div></section><section class="band"><div class="wrap"><h1>Countertop Trends We Are Seeing Right Now</h1><div class="el-text">Every year brings new directions in countertop design. Here are the six trends we are seeing most in our clients' spaces right now.</div></div></section><section class="band"><div class="wrap"><div class="el-block"><div class="el-row" style="--cols:33fr 33fr 33fr"><div class="el-col"><figure class="el-img"><img src="/images/2025/03/08mls.webp" alt="Wood cabinets with a white quartz backsplash" width="1200" height="800" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></figure><h2>Quartz Countertops — Timeless Style &amp; Low Maintenance</h2><div class="el-text"><p>Quartz countertops are available in a wide variety of styles ,including looks that rival natural stone, while being scratch-resistant and remarkably easy to maintain. Your countertops stay looking great.</p></div></div><div class="el-col"><figure class="el-img"><img src="/images/2021/10/countertop-photo-b.webp" alt="Countertop and cabinet finish samples" width="369" height="369" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></figure><h2>Quartzite Countertops — A Natural Alternative to Granite</h2><div class="el-text">Granite lovers are discovering quartzite. This natural stone has all the durability of granite but brings lighter colors and flowing, organic veining that feels fresh and current.</div></div><div class="el-col"><figure class="el-img"><img src="/images/2026/04/05.webp" alt="Walnut island with a marble top in a white kitchen" width="1200" height="800" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></figure><h2>Full-Height Backsplashes to Magnify the Drama</h2><div class="el-text">Bring the beauty of your stone countertop all the way up the wall for a dramatic, design-forward look. A full-height backsplash in the same material as your countertop creates a seamless, elevated finish.</div></div></div></div></div></section><section class="band"><div class="wrap"><div class="el-block"><div class="el-row" style="--cols:33fr 33fr 33fr"><div class="el-col"><figure class="el-img"><img src="/images/2021/10/countertop-photo-d.webp" alt="Pop-up power outlet in a quartz countertop" width="1200" height="802" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></figure><h2>Smart Hidden Outlets for Functionality</h2><div class="el-text"><p>Hidden retractable outlets are increasingly requested by our clients providing ample power when you need it &amp; a clean flat surface when you do not. </p></div></div><div class="el-col"><figure class="el-img"><img src="/images/2026/04/03.webp" alt="Long marble island with white stools under a wood ceiling" width="1200" height="800" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></figure><h2>Waterfall Islands for a Cleaner Transition</h2><div class="el-text">A waterfall edge brings the countertop material down the side of the island for a clean, continuous finish. Dramatic without being fussy.</div></div><div class="el-col"><figure class="el-img"><img src="/images/2021/10/countertop-photo-f.webp" alt="White kitchen with a granite island and white pendants" width="512" height="342" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></figure><h2>Contrasting Countertops for Texture and Interest</h2><div class="el-text"><p>A contrasting countertop on your island adds texture, visual interest and additional personality to the kitchen. It is one of the most impactful updates you can make.</p></div></div></div></div></div></section><section class="band"><div class="wrap"><p class="btn-row"><a class="btn" href="/showrooms/">View Our Project Gallery and Browse More Countertop Trends</a></p></div></section><section class="band"><div class="wrap"><div class="el-row" style="--cols:50fr 50fr"><div class="el-col"><figure class="el-img"><img src="/images/2026/06/6mls.webp" alt="White kitchen with glass-front cabinets and a stainless hood" width="1200" height="801" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></figure></div><div class="el-col"><h1>Top Countertop Styles We Carry</h1><div class="el-text"><p>Stone, quartz, quartzite, granite and more, the choice is yours. Our design experts will help you choose from a wide variety of quality materials in a range of styles and colors, all designed to fit your needs and budget.</p></div><h1>GRANITE COUNTERTOPS — THE NATURAL CHOICE</h1><div class="el-text"><p>Granite is the most popular natural stone countertop material for good reason. It comes in a wide variety of colors from vibrant blues to browns, midnight black, deep red and mottled white. Granite is extremely durable, resistant to bacteria and genuinely beautiful. If you want a natural, dramatic look that stands up to heat and daily use, granite is an excellent choice.</p></div></div></div></div></section><section class="band"><div class="wrap"><div class="el-row" style="--cols:50fr 50fr"><div class="el-col"><h1>QUARTZ &amp; QUARTZITE — THE NEW STANDARD</h1><div class="el-text"><p>Quartz countertops are engineered from ground natural quartz mixed with polymer resins resulting in a super-hard, low-maintenance, scratch-resistant surface available in a wide array of colors and styles. No resealing required and they resist staining from cooking oils, liquids and most cleaning products.</p></div><div class="el-text"><p>Quartzite is a natural metamorphic stone formed from sandstone under intense heat and pressure.  It is popular due to it's show-stopping beauty, strength and overall resilience.</p><p>Both quartz &amp; quartzite offer excellent color consistency, durability and ease of maintenance.</p></div></div><div class="el-col"><figure class="el-img"><img src="/images/2026/06/12.webp" alt="Bathroom with a wood vanity, round mirrors and a freestanding tub" width="1200" height="800" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></figure></div></div></div></section><section class="band"><div class="wrap"><h1>Visit One of Our Showrooms to See Countertops Up Close</h1><div class="el-text"><p>There is no substitute for seeing countertop materials in person. The natural variation in stone, the way light reflects across the surface and the texture you can feel are details that photos cannot capture. Stop by either of our two showrooms in the Greater New Orleans area and browse samples of the materials we carry. We're happy to walk you through your options and help you find what fits your space and budget.</p></div><div class="el-block"><div class="el-row" style="--cols:50fr 50fr"><div class="el-col"><h2>New Orleans</h2><div class="map"><iframe src="https://maps.google.com/maps?q=231%20N.%20Carrollton%20Ave%2C%20New%20Orleans&amp;t=m&amp;z=15&amp;output=embed&amp;iwloc=near" title="Map: 231 N. Carrollton Ave, New Orleans" loading="lazy"></iframe></div><div class="el-text"><p>231 N. Carrollton Ave.<br>(at Bienville, across from Brocato's)<br>New Orleans, LA 70119<br>(504) 486-0067<br>Hours: Mon-Fri 10am-5pm, Sat 10am-2pm</p></div></div><div class="el-col"><h2>Mandeville</h2><div class="map"><iframe src="https://maps.google.com/maps?q=316%20Girod%20St%20Mandeville%2C%20LA%2070448&amp;t=m&amp;z=15&amp;output=embed&amp;iwloc=near" title="Map: 316 Girod St Mandeville, LA 70448" loading="lazy"></iframe></div><div class="el-text"><p>316 Girod St.<br>(Old Mandeville)<br>Mandeville, LA 70448<br>(985) 778-2978<br>Hours: Mon-Fri 10am-5pm, Sat 10am-2pm</p></div></div></div></div></div></section>{% endraw %}{% include "partials/process-strip.njk" %}{% raw %}<section class="band"><div class="wrap"><h2>We're Here to Help You Find the Right Countertops</h2><div class="el-text"><p>Whether you want to schedule an appointment at our New Orleans or Mandeville showroom, have a question about a product we carry or would like an estimate, we'd love to talk. Our team is here to help you every step of the way.</p></div><div class="el-block"><p class="btn-row"><a class="btn" href="/request-consultation/">Let&#x27;s Talk Kitchens (504) 539-4605</a></p></div></div></section>{% endraw %}
